{
  "_about": "SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the scene-record schema. Every store derives its contract from this file: process.py's blank record, relational.py's SQLite columns/DDL/filters, search.py's named vectors (the per-field `weight` is LEGACY — search fuses summary vs svos by MAX and blends flavor by RRF method_weights, so weight no longer tunes retrieval), and the reconcile tool that ripples edits across scenes JSON + SQLite + Qdrant payloads. EDIT THIS FILE to add / rename / drop an enrichment tag, then run `python -m schema --reconcile` to make every store match. Do NOT hand-edit the derived lists in the store files.",
  "_editing": "Add a field: add an entry under `fields`. Drop a field: delete its entry (reconcile then strips it from every record; a `vector` field also needs a re-index via embed.py). `kind:core` fields are structural (ids/positions/prose/provenance) and are protected from reconcile stripping/nulling. `kind:enrichment` fields are the experimental surface (tones, frame, descriptors, summary). Field ORDER here is the SQLite column order. A `vector:true` field is a named Qdrant vector; adding `multivector:true` (a list field like svos) stores ONE vector PER item and scores by MAX_SIM max-pooling — the query's best-matching item wins, so a specific query hits a specific beat without diluting the rest. Changing multivector on/off changes the collection config and needs a full re-index (embed._ensure_collection rebuilds).",
  "schema_version": 3,
  "primary_key": "scene_id",
  "id_format": "{book_id}-{pos}",
  "indexes": [
    {"name": "ix_nav",    "cols": ["book_id", "pos"], "unique": true},
    {"name": "ix_author", "cols": ["author"]},
    {"name": "ix_lang",   "cols": ["language"]},
    {"name": "ix_tone",   "cols": ["dominant_tone"]},
    {"name": "ix_prev",   "cols": ["prev_tone"]},
    {"name": "ix_next",   "cols": ["next_tone"]},
    {"name": "ix_inten",  "cols": ["intensity"]},
    {"name": "ix_arc",    "cols": ["arc"]},
    {"name": "ix_stitch", "cols": ["stitch_status"]},
    {"name": "ix_enrich", "cols": ["enriched"]}
  ],
  "fields": {
    "scene_id":              {"kind": "core", "source": "segment", "json": true, "type": "str",  "default": null,  "sql": {"col": true, "type": "TEXT",    "store": "direct"}, "filterable": true},
    "book_id":               {"kind": "core", "source": "segment", "json": true, "type": "str",  "default": null,  "sql": {"col": true, "type": "TEXT",    "store": "direct"}, "filterable": true},
    "pos":                   {"kind": "core", "source": "derived", "json": false, "type": "int", "default": null,  "sql": {"col": true, "type": "INTEGER", "store": "pos"}},
